cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "The Endemic Baseline: When B_reference Was Never Set"
message: >-
  If you use this work in your research, please cite it using the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Brandon
    family-names: Everett
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7521-5469"
repository-code: https://github.com/YellowHapax/Endemic-Baseline
license: Apache-2.0
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-02-27"
abstract: >-
  Paper 7 in the Memory as Baseline Deviation series. Addresses the foundational
  case in which B(0) was itself constructed during chronic disruption —
  the endemic baseline. Formalizes three predicted consequences (healthy-input
  rejection, horizon invisibility, intervention failure) and derives the
  Re-zeroing Protocol from first principles. Includes two executable computational
  labs: P7a (calibration formation under healthy input) and P7b (Re-zeroing
  Protocol vs. flood vs. withdrawal).
keywords:
  - memory as baseline deviation
  - endemic baseline
  - calibration formation
  - re-zeroing protocol
  - computational psychiatry
  - MBD framework

